<title>BELGIUM: Members of WTO Helms-Burton dispute panel named.</title>
<headline>Members of WTO Helms-Burton dispute panel named.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland, New Zealand and Singapore have been nominated by World Trade Organisation chief Renato Ruggiero to sit on the dispute panel that will rule on the European Union's complaint against the United States over its Helms-Burton Act, EU sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The European Commission has been told that Arthur Dunkel of Switzerland, Ted Woodfield of New Zealand and Tommy Koh of Singapore will make up the panel,&quot; the source said. &quot;An official announcement is expected soon&quot;.</p>
</text>
